`16` members. Every target settled in the companion files *is* realised in that clone,
so no clone certificate refutes term-definability. What fails is the other half of
term-structurality: the members realising those targets generate only a proper subclone,
and `Magma.rev1875aSub` lists the `5` subclones that contain all of them. `◇` is in none
